==Personal life==

Himura maintains a residence in [[Toyozawa]]'s [[Abeno]] ward, a working-class district known for its proximity to the city's industrial waterfront. He is an avid collector of caps, having amassed over 400 items since beginning his professional career. His collection includes rare vintage OBSL merchandise, collaborations with Sanese streetwear brands, and custom-made pieces gifted by fans.

During the offseason, Himura returns to his hometown of [[Ehime]], where he operates a free youth basketball clinic at the Ehime Chuo High School gymnasium. The clinic, established in 2018, emphasizes defensive fundamentals and has produced several players who have gone on to professional careers.

Himura is known for his private nature regarding personal relationships. He has never been married and maintains no public social media presence, preferring to communicate with fans through official team channels and occasional magazine interviews.

